overage=88%, source=both]\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm vs De Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: acute myeloid leukemia, autosomal dominant inheritance, somatic mutation\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm vs Chronic Myeloid Leukemia in Blast Crisis:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal basophil morphology, abnormal granulocyte morphology, abnormal/excessive bleeding, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm vs Myelodysplastic Syndrome with Excess Blasts / Secondary AML:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal circulating albumin concentration, abnormal circulating protein concentration, abnormal mean corpuscular volume, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm vs Multiple Myeloma with Hypercalcemia:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: anemia, bone pain, constipation, frequent urination, hypercalcemia\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm vs Monoclonal Gammopathy of Undetermined Significance (MGUS) with Hypercalcemia:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: abnormal aortic morphology, abnormal aortic valve morphology, abnormal cardiac septum morphology, abnormal carotid artery morphology, abnormal eyelid morphology\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm vs Plasma Cell Leukemia (Primary or Secondary):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, arterial thrombosis, ascites\n  Favours second: 2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal obesity, abnormal cardiac septum morphology, abnormal cardiac ventricular function, abnormal cerebral white matter morphology\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia vs Chronic Myeloid Leukemia in Blast Crisis:\n  Favours first:  acute myeloid leukemia, autosomal dominant inheritance\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal basophil morphology, abnormal granulocyte morphology, abnormal/excessive bleeding, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia vs Myelodysplastic Syndrome with Excess Blasts / Secondary AML:\n  Favours first:  autosomal dominant inheritance, somatic mutation\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal circulating albumin concentration, abnormal circulating protein concentration, abnormal mean corpuscular volume, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia vs Multiple Myeloma with Hypercalcemia:\n  Favours first:  acute myeloid leukemia, autosomal dominant inheritance, somatic mutation\n  Favours second: anemia, bone pain, constipation, fatigue, frequent urination\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia vs Monoclonal Gammopathy of Undetermined Significance (MGUS) with Hypercalcemia:\n  Favours first:  acute myeloid leukemia, autosomal dominant inheritance, somatic mutation\n  Favours second: abnormal aortic morphology, abnormal aortic valve morphology, abnormal cardiac septum morphology, abnormal carotid artery morphology, abnormal eyelid morphology\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia vs Plasma Cell Leukemia (Primary or Secondary):\n  Favours first:  acute myeloid leukemia, autosomal dominant inheritance, somatic mutation\n  Favours second: 2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal obesity, abnormal cardiac septum morphology, abnormal cardiac ventricular function, abnormal cerebral white matter morphology\n\nChronic Myeloid Leukemia in Blast Crisis vs Myelodysplastic Syndrome with Excess Blasts / Secondary AML:\n  Favours first:  abdominal pain, abnormal